1
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:09,080
Right now, as you're watching this, it's
happening.

2
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:16,880
Somewhere in Africa, in the dark, in the
silence, something ancient and brutal is

3
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:23,320
unfolding. No cameras, no tourists, no
witnesses.

4
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:29,000
Every single night, Africa transforms into
a completely different world.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,560
A world most people will never see.

6
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:36,880
A world that operates by rules you were
never taught.

7
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:40,160
Tonight, we go in.

8
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:45,520
The moment the sun disappears below the
horizon, something extraordinary happens.

9
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:52,920
The animals you saw during the day, the
lions resting under trees, the elephants
slowly grazing,

10
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:54,560
they don't go to sleep.

11
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:57,240
They wake up.

12
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:00,840
Half of all animals in Africa are
nocturnal.

13
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:06,600
Half. That means every safari you've ever
seen on television showed you only half
the

14
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:11,920
story. The real Africa begins now.

15
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:17,360
Safari guides have a name for the seven
most elusive creatures of the African
night.

16
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:20,600
They call them the secret seven.

17
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:25,320
Most tourists spend weeks in Africa and
never see a single one.

18
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:31,720
There's the pangolin, covered in scales
like a medieval knight. So rare that
seeing one is

19
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:34,760
considered a once-in-a-lifetime event.

20
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:42,640
There's the aardvark, a creature so
strange that scientists still debate what
animal it's closest related to.

21
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:45,640
And then, there's the honey badger.

22
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:49,800
Pound for pound, the most fearless animal
on the planet.

23
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:55,520
It has been documented attacking full lion
prides and walking away.

24
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:58,200
These animals don't want to be found.

25
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:03,080
And that's exactly what makes them
extraordinary.

26
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:07,360
But the secret seven are just the
beginning.

27
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:11,880
Because while they hide in the shadows,
something far more dangerous has already

28
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:13,720
begun to move.

29
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:19,600
Leopards, the most secretive of all the
big cats, are primarily nocturnal hunters.

30
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:24,560
Their spotted coats become perfect
camouflage in the moonlit grass.

31
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,400
You won't hear them coming.

32
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:29,640
You won't see them until it's too late.

33
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:34,240
And lions? During the day they seem lazy,
almost peaceful.

34
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:39,400
But at night, their night vision is six
times more powerful than a human's.

35
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:44,760
A male lion's roar can travel 8 km across
the savanna.

36
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:48,880
When you hear it in the dark, the ground
vibrates beneath you.

37
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:51,800
This is the Africa nobody shows you.

38
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:54,880
This is the Africa that has no mercy.

39
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:57,040
But here's what nobody talks about.

40
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:59,800
Here's the part that will stay with you.

41
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:07,560
The African civet, a creature that looks
like a raccoon, smells like a perfume
factory, and eats literally everything,

42
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:11,400
from fruit to scorpions to venomous
snakes.

43
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:18,640
Its scent gland produces a secretion so
powerful that for centuries it was
harvested for the most expensive

44
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:26,080
perfumes in the world. The very same
animal walking silently through the
African dark was once the secret

45
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:28,360
ingredient of luxury.

46
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:35,320
Africa has always been hiding its most
valuable secrets in plain sight.

47
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:41,519
And when the predators finally rest, when
the secret seven disappear back into the
dark,

48
00:03:41,519 --> 00:03:45,760
something else happens that no camera can
fully capture.

49
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:52,160
Far from any city, far from any light, the
African sky opens up.

50
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:56,080
The Milky Way stretches from horizon to
horizon.

51
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:59,120
The Southern Cross burns bright.

52
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:03,000
You are standing in the oldest darkness on
Earth.

53
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:10,320
The same sky that our ancestors stared up
at millions of years ago, asking the same
questions we still can't

54
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:16,400
answer. Africa at night is not just a
place, it's a feeling.

55
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:21,200
It reaches inside you and reminds you of
something you forgot.

56
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:24,120
The sun will rise again in a few hours.

57
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:26,360
The lions will find their shade.

58
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:29,560
The pangolin will curl up in its burrow.

59
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:32,840
The leopard will disappear into the
canopy.

60
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:38,280
And most of the world will never know what
happened here tonight.

61
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:40,840
But now, you know.

62
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:46,720
Africa's deadliest secret isn't a place or
an animal or a predator.

63
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:48,800
It's the night itself.

64
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:54,040
If this took you somewhere you've never
been before, you know where to find more.

65
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:58,320
This is Colors of Africa.
